        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "There is a lingering question about government lawyers, including DOJ and federal government lawyers and DC prosecutors, withholding evidence.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker believes that if evidence was withheld and the Brady rule was violated, then the involved lawyers should be disbarred.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "The Brady rule requires prosecutors to disclose exculpatory evidence to the defense.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Withholding evidence by prosecutors constitutes a serious ethical violation warranting professional sanctions like disbarment.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker has sufficient trust in the legal system’s ability to enforce disciplinary actions against unethical lawyers.",
        "confidence": 0.85
      },
      {
        "text": "The public has a right to know about prosecutorial misconduct when it affects criminal justice outcomes.",
        "confidence": 0.83
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker views Tucker Carlson's viewership as indicative of media influence on political discourse.",
        "confidence": 0.79
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Topic Shift"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 83624,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/3/83624.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 64,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, if you didn't give a term of evidence, I mean, you can't do that. So certainly that is a problem. And I'll tell you what else we've learned from whistle blowers, FBI agents who've come talk to our committee staff, and three of them have been willing to sit for a transcribed interview. just the pressure, the intense pressure to go after anyone associated with January 6. We had this one whistleblower testify, where he said there was a busload of people who came down from the Boston area. He worked in the Boston field office, this FBI agent. And he said, they sent him a picture and video of the two people organized these two busloads of folks who came down. And I guess they were inside the Capitol. And so they said, we want you to open up an investigation on these two people. And they said, OK, they're inside the Capitol. We'll begin an investigation. Then they said, the other 138, we want you to open up an investigation on them too. Our whistleblower said, why? If you have any evidence that they were inside the Capitol, did something wrong? He said, no, no, we just want you to do it. He said, no, we're not going to do that. But he said, that was just one of the many examples of how intense the government went after folks who were in and around the Capitol on that particular day.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_04",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "If you don't provide a term of evidence, you cannot proceed.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "There is a significant problem with investigations lacking proper evidentiary basis.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "FBI agents faced intense pressure to investigate individuals linked to January 6.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "The whistleblower questioned the justification for investigating the additional 138 people due to lack of evidence.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Whistleblowers from the FBI have provided testimony to the committee staff.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "A specific FBI agent from the Boston field office received a photo and video of two people allegedly organizing busloads to the Capitol.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Three FBI whistleblowers have participated in transcribed interviews with the committee.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "The whistleblower refused to comply with the request to investigate the 138 individuals without evidence.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "The FBI agent was instructed to open an investigation into those two individuals because they were alleged to have been inside the Capitol.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "The FBI agent was then asked to investigate another 138 people without evidence of wrongdoing.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
