    "turn_idx": 69,
    "turn_text": "And I think, and Mr. Sun pointed this out, but I thought this from the get-go, because if you remember, Mr. Banks and I, my colleague and I, we were named to be on the committee by then leader, but now Speaker McCarthy. And there was an initial story in one of the publications here on the Hill that said, oh, the Democrats are fine with the people that that Leader McCarthy had selected for that committee. And then Mr. Banks and I started talking about how we felt that we'd seen that communication where Mr. Sun had talked about the optics of not having the National Guard in the presence here. And the fact that we weren't, we didn't have the proper security posture that day for a rally of this size. And as we started talking about then and only then did the speaker Pelosi say, oh, you guys aren't gonna be allowed to be on the committee. Because I think it all boiled down to that simple fact In the summer of 2020, we saw what happened around the country. We saw the Democrats' response. They were for decline in the police. They called it peaceful protest when it was rioters and looters. And so then to turn around and have the kind of presence you need for a rally this size, they didn't like the optics of that. And that was clear, Mr. Sun pointed that out. And I think that's why there was the lack of National Guard and others here that day.",
