    "turn_text": "At some point, I think he will be back in front of Congress. I assume it's going to happen in the select committee on the coronavirus, which I also happen to get to be a part of. That is run by Congressman Winstrope. We had our first hearing there earlier this week where Dr. Redfield really laid things out, I think, in a pretty compelling way how Fauci from the get-go. was trying to downplay and make sure no one bought into the lab league concept, the lab league theory, and was pushing that this thing came, as I've said before, from a bat to a pangolin to a hip eponymous to Joe Rogan and then, you know, coronavirus goes everywhere. So when we all know that it was, you know, and the reason he was so focused on that being is because Fauci knew right from the start that he had sent our tax dollars to a lab in China that wasn't up to code that was doing gain of function research. And the virus starts in that same city where that labs at. And he's like, oh sugar, I got to do something. I got to keep that from getting out. And he knew it had to come from a lab because the first email he gets on January 31st, 2020, 1032 p.m. from Dr. Christian Anderson says what? Virus looks engineered, virus inconsistent with evolutionary theory. That is a fancy way of saying it came from that lab. And he goes into overdrive to cover his backside and a bunch of things happen over the next few days. And that same doctor who said that on January 31st on February 3rd says you're a nut job if you think it came from a lab. Switch is 180 degrees. And I think the only thing happened is Dr. Fauci got to him and said, hey, dude, we got to get our story straight because I can't have this stuff getting out. We can't have this stuff getting out. And then Christian Anderson and another doctor who said the same thing, they get a $9 million grant three months later.",
