    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/3/83624.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 98,
    "turn_text": "I don't know that Mr. Comer on the oversight committee, Chairman Comer is going to pursue this issue. Our focus in judiciary is to the degree and influence that the FBI may have had on how this story broke back in 2020. We got into this yesterday in our hearing in the select committee. But, you know, the FBI for a year. And this is Joel Roth, a head of trust and safety at Twitter under his sworn declaration. He says, for a year, I had meetings with ODNI, FBI, DHS. We had these weekly meetings, sometimes even more often than as I got closer to the election. They were telling me that to be on the lookout for a hack and leak operation that it would happen in October of 2020 and it would involve Hunter Biden. And I'm like, I mean, the FBI, and then it happens. So the FBI had predicted the type of operator, the method, and the person. I'm like, how did they do that? How did the FBI know that there's going to be a hacking leak in October of 2020 involving Hunter Biden? And I think they knew because they had the laptop. So they were telling them something, even though they had the laptop that they knew was all authentic. Our involvement, I think, is the involvement of the Justice Department in furthering this narrative that they had the laptop. So they furthered this narrative, that's the hack and leak, and they knew that the laptop wasn't. So that's where we're going to focus on our committee.",
